<title>BAHRAIN: ABC H1 97 profit rises.</title>
<headline>ABC H1 97 profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>MANAMA 1997-08-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Arab Banking Corp (ABC) said on Saturday its pre-tax profit in the first half of 1997 rose to $94 million from $88 million in the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>The bank, one of the largest in the Arab world, said in a statement operating profit for the period was $161 million, up from $117 million in the same period of 1996.</p>
<p>It said its loans and advances stood at $11.5 billion on June 30, 1997 compared to $10.9 billion a year earlier. Total assets increased to $23.2 billion from $21.5 billion.</p>
<p>Shares of the Bahrain-based bank are traded on the Bahraini, Paris and Kuwaiti bourses.</p>
<p>-- Bahrain newsroom 973-424424</p>
